    'A sequence has the property that each term is 1 or 2 and repeats with period p. If p divides 2^k for some k, and we observe 2^10+1 terms, how many terms guarantee seeing every pattern of length 10?',
    '1025',
    'exact',
    '2^10+1=1025',
    '2^10+1=1025 terms to guarantee all 2^10 patterns of length 10 appear',
    6500,
    '[{"level": 1, "text": "Can you pair up or group the items into categories? How many categories are there?", "cost": 0}, {"level": 2, "text": "The Pigeonhole Principle: if you have more items than categories, at least one category must contain 2 or more items.", "cost": 5}, {"level": 3, "text": "Count the categories, then figure out how many items force at least one category to overflow. The formula is: (categories \u00d7 max per category) + 1.", "cost": 15}]'::jsonb,
    'Pigeonhole: more pigeons than holes → at least one hole has 2 pigeons! Existence without finding it.',
    'The pigeonhole principle proves things must happen without showing exactly where.',
    ARRAY['number_theory', 'pigeonhole', 'combinatorics', 'zone-5'],
    10,
    3
);

