    '[{"level": 1, "text": "Can you count pairs? Each pair is counted once. How many pairs can be formed from n things?", "cost": 0}, {"level": 2, "text": "Use the triangular number formula: 1+2+3+\u2026+n = n(n+1)\u00f72. Identify what n is in this problem.", "cost": 5}, {"level": 3, "text": "Find n (the total number of people or items), then compute n\u00d7(n\u22121)\u00f72 for pairs, or n\u00d7(n+1)\u00f72 for the sum 1 to n.", "cost": 15}]'::jsonb,
    'Triangular numbers: n(n+1)/2. Handshakes, sums, pairs — all the same formula!',
    'Gauss''s trick: pairing 1+n, 2+(n−1), etc. gives n/2 pairs each summing to n+1.',
    ARRAY['sequences', 'triangular-numbers', 'handshakes', 'combinations', 'zone-1'],
    17,
    2
);

